SUMMARY:The 1977 Disaster at Tenerife (LECTURE ON THE GO)
DESCRIPTION:Toronto History Walks\n**The Toronto History Walks Explorer Pa
 ss is available. Get it now for $125.00 for 1 year of unlimited tours\, em
 ail**\n**torontohistorywalks@gmail.com**\n**for more information or for si
 gning up!**\n\nWe have an amazing "Lecture on the Go" series for 2026. New
  topics and fascinating stories abound! Join me\, and uncover the world an
 d keep active\, warm and cool during the winter and summer months!\n\nI st
 arted this walking classroom when we were under that horrible cloud called
  Covid. This series was popular and helped people get back into society an
 d life.\n\nThe "Lecture on the Go" Series is open to members who have purc
 hased the YEARLY MEMBERSHIP PASS\, it's free for those members. If you wis
 h to attend a lecture and you are not a yearly pass member then the price 
 **per** lecture is $20.00.\n\nOn March 27\, 1977\, Tenerife\, an island ch
 ain off the west coast of Africa\, became the stage for the most devastati
 ng aviation disaster in history. Two fully loaded 747 aircraft collided on
  the same runway. What began as a series of circumstances\, diverted fligh
 ts\, dense fog\, quickly spiralled into a chain of misunderstandings that 
 would change aviation forever. This story is not just about the disaster\,
  but about human factors\, and the communication breakdowns\, which led to
  it. And in today's modern AI landscape we are again under threat.\n\nAt t
 he heart of the tragedy\, language\, hierarchy\, and timing\, where small 
 misinterpretations carried enormous consequences. The Tenerife disaster wa
 s far more than an accident\; it's a powerful case study in how systems\, 
 and people fail.\n\nJoin me as we step back onto that fog-shrouded runway 
 and piece together the events\, decisions\, and lessons of that day.\n\nTh
 is lecture goes beyond the headlines to uncover the human stories\, the te
 chnical realities\, and the lasting changes that reshaped global aviation.
  Are we safer\, yes\, but for how long? That is a matter for discussion.\n
 \nUpcoming topics in the 2026 series:\n\n\\*Philosophy 1: Great Minds of t
 he Western World: Goethe to Kant! - (June 2026)\n\\*Philosophy 2: Great Mi
 nds of the Eastern\nWorld: Chuang Tzu to Dalai Lama - (July 2026)\nLegacy 
 of Triangle: How a New York Factory Scandal changed North America - (Septe
 mber 2026)\n\nThis is the fifth event in the series! So book your plans no
 w!\n\nThis event is for all levels and walkers\, there are a few steps her
 e and there to navigate\, but mostly on one level. This event in a non-wal
 king event.\n\nThe lecture begins on the steps of Old City Hall at the nor
 theast corner of Bay Street and Queen Street West\, and\nhas a ticket pric
 e of $20.00 per person\, but **free with the yearly membership pass**.\n\n
 **Please note: Please e-transfer the ticket amount when booking your space
  for this tour! You can e-transfer to the following email at:**\n**toronto
 historywalks@gmail.com**
