BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Meetup: History of Parkdale
UID:event_315254187@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20260808T022707Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260816T133000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260816T153000
SUMMARY:South Core and Sugar Beach
DESCRIPTION:Toronto History Walks\n**The Toronto History Walks Yearly Pass
  is available. Get it now for $125.00 for 1 year of unlimited tours\, emai
 l**\n[torontohistorywalks@gmail.com](http://torontohistorywalks@gmail.com%
 2A%2A/)\n**for more information or for signing up!**\n\n**Please note: Ple
 ase e-transfer the ticket amount when booking your space for this tour! Yo
 u can e-transfer to the following email at:**\n[torontohistorywalks@gmail.
 com](http://torontohistorywalks@gmail.com%2A%2A/)\n\nSouth Core is a new a
 nd up and coming district centred on Lower Jarvis Street and Queen's Quay 
 East.\n\nOnce an industrial area of the old port lands\, South Core has be
 come a new and exciting destination for residents and tourists alike. With
  walking paths adjacent and Sugar Beach on the waterfront\, South Core is 
 the place to stroll and learn about Toronto's history. This tour should be
  called "Back to the 50's."\n\nBut it also has a rather interesting histor
 y. Let's start with the Redpath Sugar complex which opened in 1958. Adjace
 nt to Sugar Beach\, several port facilities were built including the Queen
  Elizabeth Terminals for unloading produce entering Canada. With the openi
 ng of the St. Lawrence Seaway\, Toronto built several more terminals which
  have been converted to residences. Grab a coffee and relax in a most inte
 resting part of Toronto.\n\nThis walk is for all fitness levels. The meeti
 ng place for our walking adventure is the northwest corner of Sugar Beach 
 on Queen's Quay East east at Lower Jarvis Street. See you there! We will e
 nd at Cherry Street amid the new development there with the widening of th
 e Don River\, and all that glorious parkland! Let's explore\, on the perfe
 ct summer walk!\n\nThis tour has a ticket price of $15.00 per person!\n\n\
 \*\\* **Please note: Please e-transfer the ticket price when booking your 
 space for this tour! You can e-transfer to the following email at:**\n\\*\
 \*[torontohistorywalks@gmail.com**](http://torontohistorywalks@gmail.com%2
 A%2A/)
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/the-history-of-parkdale/events/315254
 187/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260614T125343Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260614T125343Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Meetup: History of Parkdale
UID:event_315583572@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20260808T022707Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260820T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260820T130000
SUMMARY:Historic Buildings Walking Tour!
DESCRIPTION:Toronto History Walks\n\\*\\***The Toronto History Walks Explo
 rer Pass is available. Get it now for $125.00 for 1 year of unlimited tour
 s\, email**\n**torontohistorywalks@gmail.com**\n**for more information or 
 for signing up!\\*\\***\n\n\\*\\* **Please note: Please e-transfer the tic
 ket amount when booking your space for this tour! You can e-transfer to th
 e following email at:**\n**torontohistorywalks@gmail.com**\n\nToronto has 
 a rich history\, and it's all around us\, but certain buildings do stand o
 ut and tell our story. On this walking tour the following buildings are ex
 plored and their history revealed. This new tour is for residents and tour
 ists who want to reconnect with their city\, or get to know it from a diff
 erent vantage point!\n\n* Daniel Brooke Building\n* St. Lawrence Hall\n* S
 t. James Anglican Cathedral\n* St. Michael's Cathedral\n* Mackenzie House\
 n* Massey Hall\n* Old City Hall\n* Osgoode Hall\n* Campbell House Museum\n
 * Gooderham Building\n\nand a few other hidden surprises along the way fro
 m the Toronto Stock Exchange to the New City Hall and a few others in betw
 een!\n\nThis walking tour is for all walking levels. Please dress for the 
 season\, and hope to see you there.\n\nPlease meet in front of the iconic 
 St. Lawrence Hall at the corner of Jarvis and King Street East\, we end th
 e tour at Historic Campbell House!\n\nThis tour has a ticket price of $15.
 00 per person.\n\n\\*\\* **Please note: Please e-transfer the ticket amoun
 t when booking your space for this tour! You can e-transfer to the followi
 ng email at:**\n**torontohistorywalks@gmail.com**
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/the-history-of-parkdale/events/315583
 572/
